      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2.2. Experimental details",
          "quote": "The alloy ingots of these four compositions were prepared using vacuum arc melting in a water-cooled copper hearth under an argon atmosphere. Prior to melting, the raw materials (Mo, Nb, Ta, V, and Al) with a purity of 99.99 % were mechanically ground to remove the surface oxidation and then ultrasonically cleaned in ethanol for 3 min. High-purity Ti was employed as a degassing substance to remove residual oxygen in the vacuum chamber. In order to ensure chemical homogeneity, the button ingots were remelted for six times.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "7a8360160faebf6d:part:001"
